@* OnThisPage's Overview, written by hand after Badge's: the guide demo (previewed in each mode),
   which levels it lists, headings the server can't see, and pages without an AppShell.
   Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>An on-this-page outline is a list of a long page's sections beside it, so the user sees what's there and can jump to a section. It suits long guides and reference pages. The list is in the server's response, so it works with <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>; with IzzyBlazor's script, it marks the section in view as the page scrolls.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>For links between pages, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/nav-menu">NavMenu</Anchor> in the sidebar and <Anchor Href="docs/components/prev-next">PrevNext</Anchor> at the end of each page.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A guide with its outline</Heading>
<TextBlock>A guide's outline sits in the aside, beside the article. Put OnThisPage in an <Code>AppAside</Code>. Each <Anchor Href="docs/components/heading">Heading</Anchor> in <Code>AppMain</Code> adds itself while the page renders, with an id taken from its text, so its link works with no setup.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="on-this-page-guide" />
<TextBlock>The aside shows from its <Code>Breakpoint</Code> up, 1024px by default. This example sets it lower to fit the window.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Which headings</Heading>
<TextBlock>OnThisPage lists h2 and h3 headings by default, with each level indented under the one above. To list other levels, such as only h2 on a page of short sections, set <Code>MinLevel</Code> and <Code>MaxLevel</Code>, from 1 to 6.</TextBlock>
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>Only headings in the main area are listed, not those in the header, the sidebar or the aside.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>To leave a heading out, such as one inside a card or a dialog, set <Code>OnThisPage="false"</Code> on it.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>With no headings to list, OnThisPage is hidden, so there's no empty landmark.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Headings the server doesn't see</Heading>
<TextBlock>Headings written as HTML, such as those in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/prose">Prose</Anchor> block or rendered Markdown, aren't components, so the server can't list them. IzzyBlazor's script adds the ones that have an id, in page order. With JavaScript off, they're left out, so use <Code>Heading</Code> for the important sections.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Without an AppShell</Heading>
<TextBlock>The list comes from the AppShell, which collects the headings in its <Code>AppMain</Code>. On a page with no AppShell, the server lists nothing and renders OnThisPage hidden. IzzyBlazor's script then lists the headings that have an id in the page's <Code>main</Code> element.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Headings get ids from their text only in an AppShell, so give each heading an <Code>id</Code> on such a page.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The outline has a heading of its own. To set it for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Title</Code></td><td>The outline's heading, which also names its landmark</td><td>"On this page"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

